  "rationale": "The workflow runs on push and pull_request with no concurrency control, so repeated pushes to the same branch/PR let stale runs consume runner time while a newer revision is already validating. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE (cancel superseded runs) is evidence-supported for workflows where runs represent the same workflow/branch/PR and a newer revision supersedes older checks. Adding a top-level concurrency group keyed by workflow and ref with cancel-in-progress cancels in-progress superseded runs while preserving every build and test step, all required checks, permissions, and network use unchanged. This is a test workflow (not release/deployment), and grouping by github.ref keeps distinct branches isolated, matching the pattern's preconditions and avoiding its contraindications.",
